{"records":[{"id":"835fcfbvhs","title":"Preparation of CRISPR/Cas9 and gRNA plasmids","description":"Human genome engineering has been transformed by the introduction of the CRISPR (clustered regularly interspaced short palindromic repeats)/Cas (CRISPR-associated) system found in most bacteria and archaea. Type II CRISPR/Cas systems have been engineered to induce RNA-guided genome editing in human cells, where small RNAs function together with Cas9 nucleases for sequence-specific cleavage of target sequences. Here we describe the protocol for Cas9-mediated human genome engineering, including construct building and transfection methods necessary for delivering Cas9 and guide RNA (gRNA) into human-induced pluripotent stem cells (hiPSCs) and HEK293 cells. Following genome editing, we also describe methods to assess genome editing effi- ciency using next-generation sequencing and isolate monoclonal hiPSCs with the desired modifications for downstream applications. Keywords: genome engineering • CRISPR • human stem cells","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2016-12-12T12:58:15.307Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/835fcfbvhs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/835fcfbvhs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"George","last_name":"Church","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Experimental Method"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"33tm3dd9dw","title":"FAME-CRISPR: Improved CRISPR-Cas9 Genome Editing via HDAC Inhibition and Engineered Virus-Like Particle Delivery ","description":"Raw data deposited for \"FAME-CRISPR: Improved CRISPR-Cas9 Genome Editing via HDAC Inhibition and Engineered Virus-Like Particle Delivery\" by Djamshidi et al-Cell Reports Methods","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-09-25T15:53:30.358Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/33tm3dd9dw","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/33tm3dd9dw"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mahbod","last_name":"Djamshidi","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Sanger Sequencing","Immunofluorescence"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3ctpx4k6jp","title":"Porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus upregulates SMPDL3B to promote viral replication by modulating lipid metabolism","description":"We generated a collection of porcine genome-scale CRISPR/Cas9 knockout (PigGeCKO) cells on a PAM background.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-26T18:53:54.241Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3ctpx4k6jp","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3ctpx4k6jp"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"huanh","last_name":"Shen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Agricultural Biotechnology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"vs9fwhbcvj","title":"Genome-wide Brie CAD5 Surface PrPC - Differentiated PrPC High","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 KO library (Brie) performed in differentiated CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_High to indicate that these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC High\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the biological replicates function to compare between \"PrP Low\" and \"PrP High\" samples.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:42.171Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vs9fwhbcvj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vs9fwhbcvj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"p5t6d78zn8","title":"Genome-wide Brie CAD5 Surface PrPC - Differentiated PrPC Low","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 KO library (Brie) performed in differentiated CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_Low  to indicate that these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC Low\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the biological replicates function to compare between \"PrP Low\" and \"PrP High\" samples.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:58.456Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/p5t6d78zn8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/p5t6d78zn8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"4r55hvz87r","title":"Negative DNA supercoiling induces genome-wide Cas9 off-target activity. Newton MD et al","description":"CRISPR/Cas9 is a powerful gene-editing technology, however off-target activity remains an important consideration for therapeutic applications. We have previous-ly shown that force stretching DNA induces off-target activity and hypothesised that distortions of the DNA topology in vivo, such as negative DNA supercoiling, could reduce Cas9 specificity. Using single-molecule optical-tweezers, we demonstrate that negative supercoiling λ-DNA induces sequence-specific Cas9 off-target bind-ing at multiple sites, even at low forces. Using an adapted CIRCLE-seq approach, we detect over 10,000 negative supercoiling induced Cas9 off-target double-strand breaks genome wide, caused by increased mismatch tolerance. We further demon-strate in vivo that directed local DNA distortion increases off-target activity in cells and that induced off-target events can be detected during Cas9 genome-editing. These data demonstrate that Cas9 off-target activity is regulated by DNA topology in vitro and in vivo, suggesting that cellular processes, such as transcription and replication, could induce off-target activity at previously overlooked sites. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-03-12T08:20:22.495Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/4r55hvz87r","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/4r55hvz87r"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Matt","last_name":"Newton","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Biochemistry","Molecular Biology","Single Molecule Imaging","Next Generation Sequencing","CRISPR/Cas9","Genome Editing"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"v4zbbbsr5t","title":"VPS33A and VPS18 orchestrate porcine epidemic diarrhea virus replication by modulating autophagic flux","description":"Completion of autophagy through autophagosome-lysosome fusion represents a critical regulatory checkpoint that is frequently manipulated during viral infection, yet how coronaviruses exploit this terminal step remains incompletely understood. Porcine epidemic diarrhea virus (PEDV), a highly pathogenic alphacoronavirus, has been reported to induce autophagy, but whether and how complete autophagic flux contributes to viral replication is unclear. Here, using a genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 knockout screen in Vero cells, we identify the HOPS complex subunits VPS33A and VPS18 as essential host factors for PEDV infection. Genetic ablation of either VPS33A or VPS18 profoundly suppresses viral progeny production and arrests autophagic flux at the autophagosome stage, demonstrating that PEDV replication is associated with HOPS-mediated autolysosome formation. Domain-mapping analyses further reveal that the structural integrity of VPS33A and the α-solenoid plus RING domains of VPS18 are indispensable for both autophagosome-lysosome fusion and efficient viral replication. Mechanistically, we show that PEDV non-structural proteins nsp3 and nsp4 physically interact with VPS33A and VPS18. While either protein alone initiates autophagosome formation, their coordinated action contributes to drive complete autophagy in a HOPS-dependent manner. Collectively, our findings uncover a coronavirus strategy that actively promotes autophagic completion through VPS33A and VPS18, two core subunits of the HOPS complex, to support replication, thereby establishing autolysosome formation as a critical host process exploited by PEDV.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-05-18T15:12:38.75Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/v4zbbbsr5t","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/v4zbbbsr5t"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"liang","last_name":"guo","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":null,"name":"the National Key Research and Development Program of China","grant_id":"2023YFC3404301, 2023YFF1000204, and 2021YFA0805901"},{"id":null,"name":"the Hainan Provincial Natural Science Foundation of China","grant_id":"323QN261"}],"categories":["Virus","Animal"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"66ms37y66x","title":"Data for: A genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 screen reveals that riboflavin regulates hydrogen peroxide entry into HAP1 cells  ","description":"CRISPR screen data for hydrogen peroxide mediated cell death","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-02-13T14:30:16.414Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/66ms37y66x","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/66ms37y66x"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"surachai","last_name":"supattapone","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kenneth","last_name":"Mark","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Tamutenda","last_name":"Chidawanyika","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Oxidative Stress"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"hbr8p7n526","title":"Cross-regulation between TDP-43 and paraspeckles promotes pluripotency-differentiation transition. Modic et al","description":"Sanger sequencing and confirmatory gel electrophoresis confirming the CRISPR-Cas9 edited human and mouse embryonic stem cells presented in the manuscript under review entitled \"Cross-regulation between TDP-43 and paraspeckles promotes pluripotency-differentiation transition\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-03-19T17:58:48.63Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/hbr8p7n526","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/hbr8p7n526"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"micha","last_name":"drukker","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["DNA Sequencing","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"9zcsxg8ncs","title":"Data for: Quantitative proteome analysis identifies MAP2K6 as potential regulator of LIFR-induced radioresistance in nasopharyngeal carcinoma cells","description":"The quantification reproducibility was investigated and Pearson correlation diagrams for the identified proteins in CEN and CNE-IR cells.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-10-08T08:04:49.905Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/9zcsxg8ncs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/9zcsxg8ncs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Liangfang","last_name":"Shen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Oncology","Radiation","Nasopharyngeal Cancer"],"journal_issn":["0006291X"]}],"total_records":109267,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":94,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":109267,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":108805,"restricted":53,"embargoed":409},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":1905},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":575},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":427},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":367},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":365},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":365},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":341},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":294},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":235},{"id":"https://ror.org/00k4n6c32","name":"European Commission","count":192}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":106738},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1888},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":172},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":112},{"id":"df228bbb-ac66-410f-8c66-f61608d63d95","name":"University of 